// t_7cc742ed.  Measured against sce-cgc 475.
// A FORM FEED IS NOT A SEPARATOR, IT IS INVALID INPUT.  The whitespace rule
// this slice introduces stopped treating everything \s matches as separating
// the name from the body; form feed and vertical tab are the two characters
// where that is observable.  Read as function-like the bare K refused (which
// agreed with the reference by accident); read as object-like it ACCEPTED,
// which does not.  Found by codex on the first revision.
//
// The reference refuses these characters ANYWHERE in a source - even
// `return<FF>t*2.0;` in ordinary code - so this is not a #define rule; the
// general form is carded and what is pinned here is the acceptance this slice
// introduced.  Reference: error C0000: syntax error, unexpected $undef.
#define K(1.0)
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return t * K; }
